message: "If you use or build on this work, please cite it as below."
type: report
title: "Putting Plastic on a Pedestal: Experimental methods of plastic waste reduction for 3D printing"
version: "1.0"
date-released: 2026-11-10
authors:
  - family-names: Armstrong
    given-names: Matthew
    alias: The-Dorkknight
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/The-Dorkknight/putting-plastic-on-a-pedestal"
url: "https://github.com/The-Dorkknight/putting-plastic-on-a-pedestal"
abstract: >-
  A defensive publication describing hollow-tower "pedestal" supports with wide filleted lobe heads, a
  four-layer interface cap rewritten into the G-code, and wall-to-wall tether supports with a simulated
  span limit, implemented as the Cura plug-in Hybrid Supports. Sliced (not printed) on 200 x 200 mm parts,
  the pedestals use 64 to 84 % less support plastic than Cura's normal support. Physically untested.
keywords:
  - 3D printing
  - FDM
  - support structures
  - Cura
  - defensive publication
  - material reduction
